# Code identity of the X570 tree that ran the mismatched-splits sweep on
# gfx1201
#
# Captured 2026-09-06, card idle at 0% and no python runner alive, before
# the sweep started. Two files were synced in beforehand --
# scripts/campaign_mismatched_splits.sh and
# docs/prereg-mismatched-splits.md -- and every other file is as the
# step-level sweep of 2026-09-05 left it. In particular
# src/burstserve/runtime.py is still 139b944^, before the
# max_steps_per_round flag, which is the pin that keeps every hardware
# campaign here commensurable. This sweep does not use the runtime.
#
# scripts/run_amd_nway_steps.py hashes identical to dd's copy, checked
# before launch:
#   e7f7c5c46870c4b68935dcbeba3d976562f400399abb0d0f083cefc628dfd579
#
# What this sweep exists to settle: whether claim 1.5 survives on the
# device it was measured on. 1.5's harness reads last_step_seconds every
# iteration and that attribute goes stale (3.10); 1.12 reads 4.93 on
# gfx90a where 1.5 reads 1.00-1.06. The sweep re-measures the same-model
# comparator in the same session, because the five same-model pairs
# already on disk are from the pre-fix instrument and their allocator
# control fails -- 2048 ms against a solo_before of 504 at eight ways.
# Verdicts and the invalidation rule are fixed in
# docs/prereg-mismatched-splits.md, written before the first cell.
#
