# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Amended 2026-09-06, mid-campaign, after nine of thirteen runs.
#
# `mm_16_16` wrote its output file and printed its verdict, then sat in
# `kfd_wait_on_events` with its CPU clock frozen and the GPU at 3% for
# 35 minutes. `--diagnose` destroys the peer streams with
# `hipStreamDestroy` while torch still holds them, and at interpreter
# teardown something waits on an event belonging to a stream that no
# longer exists. SIGTERM cleared it and the card came back to 0% -- this
# is not the 2026-09-05 wedge, which was a device-wide sync from eight
# threads and survived the kill.
#
# Two files changed before the remaining four runs:
#
#   scripts/run_amd_nway_steps.py
#     was  e7f7c5c46870c4b68935dcbeba3d976562f400399abb0d0f083cefc628dfd579
#     now  800be9bbfe498c87aeef9e6affb1799af5df487bd9f8791ec446907ceafdf910
#     diff: sys.stdout.flush(); sys.stderr.flush(); os._exit(0) after the
#     final flushed print, plus the comment explaining why. It runs
#     strictly after args.out.write_text(), so no measured quantity in
#     this campaign or any earlier one can differ because of it.
#
#   scripts/campaign_mismatched_splits.sh
#     was  405ccf4a2087af45a9b98073bce4fcbbc87cddcb307130485bb22a664b432b5f
#     now  3647263eac6fbcc27db3cbb1ea44ebd765e0202b273e53ae778672ba16127712
#     diff: the per-run check is now "was the file written" rather than
#     the python exit status. Killing the hung run returned 143 and the
#     `|| exit 1` took the remaining four cells with it.
#
# So runs solo_cog_32, same_sdxl_{4_28,8_24,16_16,24_8,28_4} and
# mm_{4_28,8_24,16_16} were produced by the first hash and
# mm_{24_8,28_4}, mm_16_16_rev and same_cog_16_16 by the second. The
# nine already on disk were NOT re-run: nothing about them changed, and
# re-running them would have replaced evidence rather than added any.
